---
title: Model Configuration
name: Model Configuration
description: Per-model options for security, fields, relations, search, filters and sorting.
---

The `models` option overrides behavior per model, keyed by Prisma model name
when using Prisma, or by the model names returned by a custom adapter.

```typescript
models: {
  User: {
    hidden: ['password', 'hashedPassword'],
    readonly: ['id', 'createdAt', 'updatedAt'],
    listFields: ['email', 'name', 'role', 'createdAt'],
    label: 'Users',
    scope: ({ locals }) => ({ organizationId: locals.organizationId }),
    searchFields: ['email', 'name'],
    listFilter: ['role', 'active'],
    defaultSort: { field: 'name', dir: 'asc' },
    relations: {
      organization: { widget: 'select', where: ({ locals }) => ({ id: locals.organizationId }) }
    }
  }
}
```

## `hidden`

Fields listed here never appear in the admin — not in list views, create/edit
forms, audit payloads or plugin record payloads. Use this for secrets and fields
you do not want rendered under any circumstance.

## `readonly`

Fields listed here are shown in edit forms but cannot be changed. This is useful
for IDs, timestamps, or anything else that should be visible but immutable.

## `listFields`

Controls which columns appear in the list view. Without it, the admin shows the
first six eligible fields. An explicit entry can override a false positive from
the automatic sensitive-name heuristic; `hidden` still wins.

## `label`

Overrides the display name used throughout the admin UI. Defaults to the model
name.

## `scope` and `listWhere`

Use `scope` for tenant authorization. It applies to every admin read and
mutation, including detail, edit, delete, dashboard counts, relations and
plugins. Scoped creates impose equality values and fail closed when the tenant
context is missing or ambiguous.

`listWhere` is list-only: it narrows list/search/filter/pagination results but
never protects direct detail or mutation URLs. Use it for presentation filters,
not authorization. Both scopes compose with `AND`; an empty scope throws rather
than failing open. See [Configuration Reference](/docs/configuration-reference).

## `relations`

Configure relation widgets, labels, ordering and option scoping. Supported
widgets are `select`, `raw-id` and `hidden`; many-to-many relations render
checkboxes by default. See [Relations](/docs/relations).

## `searchFields` and `listFilter`

`searchFields` explicitly selects fields for free-text search. `listFilter`
configures the sidebar filters; Boolean and enum fields can also be detected
automatically. See [Search & Filters](/docs/search-filters).

## `defaultSort`

Sets the initial order for a list before a visitor chooses a `?sort=` value. The
field must be displayed by `listFields` (or be eligible for the default list),
and `dir` defaults to `asc`.
